Reason:  
• It builds the cohort from users who both fired a quick‑play event between 2‑Jul and 16‑Jul AND had at least one `session_start` in that same window (matches “focus on users who started a session … during this period”).  
• Retention is measured with a `session_start` exactly 14 days after the first quick‑play, which is the standard way to express user retention; the task talks about “retention rate … two weeks after”, not about performing another quick‑play.  
• The alternative query (2result.sql) counts a return only if the user performs another quick‑play event, ignoring `session_start`s, so it does not answer the stated requirement.